From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Drag files out of the Shell

Files shown by the Shell could not be dragged anywhere: the Shell's own
drag and drop never reaches a client. lumaFileDrag.js drags them with
Mutter's MetaDataDrag (mutter 0031), a compositor-owned Wayland drag, so
any surface that shows files can hand them to Filer, GTK and Qt
applications, Flatpak applications through the document portal, browser
drop zones and X11 applications, exactly as a drag from Filer would.

The drag offers Filer's types in Filer's order: paths as text, the URI
list and a document portal FileTransfer key (StartTransfer with O_PATH
descriptors from shell_util_open_paths(), stopped after the drag). Shift
moves and Control copies; a plain drop copies. Over the Shell the drag
uses the same targets as a drag from Filer (xdndHandler): an
application's dock tile opens the files, and a dock folder now takes
files in through Filer's FileOperations2 (with a GIO fallback). The
cursor and the drag image show whether the Shell would take the drop.

A pointer press becomes a drag past 8 px, so a click stays a click; a
touch drag starts with a long press, and moving first scrolls. The drag
image is a stack of the files' faces with a count, hidden from pick.

Dock folders: Stack rows, Grid cells and the desktop panel's cards are
drag sources. Control-click and Shift-click select, and dragging a
selected item drags the selection. While the drag runs the surface is
transparent and lets the pointer through; a drop closes an attached
surface, a cancel brings it back.
---
